            <ArticleTitle>Malunion of the ulnar styloid as a cause of ulnar wrist pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>418-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of ulnar wrist pain that had been wrongly attributed to non-union of the ulnar styloid. Surgical exploration revealed an ulnar styloid malunion that had caused pain by impinging on the triquetrum and a triangular fibrocartilage complex (TFC) lesion. There was no fracture of the distal radius and no associated carpal instability or disruption of the distal radio-ulnar joint. Treatment by resection of the ulnar styloid and re-attachment of the TFC provided a satisfactory outcome.</AbstractText>
